  "prefLabel": "Rev 1501.11 Preferred stock",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1501.11 “Preferred stock” means a class of stock ownership in a corporation that has a higher claim on the assets and earnings than common stock, has a dividend that must be paid out before common stock dividends, and typically does not have voting rights.\n\nSource. #10662, eff 8-27-14; ss by #13977, eff 5-23-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1500.html"
